<title>SPAIN: Spain not planning indirect tax rise, despite EMU.</title>
<headline>Spain not planning indirect tax rise, despite EMU.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Spanish government has no plans to raise indirect taxes either this year or next, Secretary of the Exchequer Juan Costa said on Monday.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for the secretary confirmed the government is not planning to raise indirect taxes even if the European Commission approves a fiscal harmonisation plan which theoretically would increase taxes on diesel and petrol.</p>
<p>Speaking in Valencia, Costa said the government would make efforts so that &quot;price performance is appropriate and allows us to fulfil our targets, so we don't expect to apply modifications which affect this aim.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
